  "details": "The pupil movement behavior is different between conventional IK and 2.0 IK.\nWith IK 2.0, if the head is close to the ground (like in a prone position), the pupils will try to look upwards, and this cannot be disabled. If you revert to traditional IK, you will be able to face the front correctly.\nI know there are few users like me who are active close to the ground, but I hope this can be improved so that I can face the front.",
